From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kk: declare registers after the SSA temporaries

fxgl/steamac 0090 (after v1.9.7) declares NIR registers at function
scope, with the SSA temporaries, so that a value can cross the guarded
sibling blocks it emits for selections nested deeper than 128. It put
each declaration where its decl_reg comes in the walk over the
instructions, which is first; before, the declaration was printed in the
body, right after the temporaries.

The two orders mean the same, but Metal compiles them to code that
rounds differently. Replaying a 30-frame capture of MSFS 2024 (A380X
cockpit, 4224 shaders, 2997 of them with registers; shader disk cache
off) every frame differed from the same replay without 0090: up to
10/255 on a channel, up to 2.9% of the pixels of a frame, growing over
the frames as the differences feed temporal passes. Both are valid
results, but a pixel comparison across driver versions is how changes
here are checked, and it cannot tell that noise from a regression.

Registers are still declared at function scope, now after the
temporaries. The MSL of all 4224 shaders is the same text as without
0090 and the 30 frames are equal pixel for pixel; steamac's
sentry-g-brackets repro (ladder, nested, jumps, alu) still passes.

Applies after 0016.
---
 src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
index 6eab7998103..3d1728f2e08 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
@@ -3350,12 +3350,9 @@ predeclare_ssa_values(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_function_impl *impl)
          }
          case nir_instr_type_intrinsic: {
             nir_intrinsic_instr *intr = nir_instr_as_intrinsic(instr);
-            if (intr->intrinsic == nir_intrinsic_decl_reg) {
-               const char *type = msl_uint_type(nir_intrinsic_bit_size(intr),
-                                               nir_intrinsic_num_components(intr));
-               P_IND(ctx, "%s r%u = %s(0);\n", type, intr->def.index, type);
+            /* Declared after the SSA temporaries, below */
+            if (intr->intrinsic == nir_intrinsic_decl_reg)
                continue;
-            }
             if (!instrinsic_needs_dest_type(intr))
                continue;
             def = &intr->def;
@@ -3386,6 +3383,26 @@ predeclare_ssa_values(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_function_impl *impl)
          }
       }
    }
+
+   /* Registers go after the SSA temporaries, which is where their decl_reg
+    * (first in the first block) put them before fxgl/steamac 0090 moved them
+    * to function scope: the MSL of a shader without deep selections stays
+    * the same text as before. Metal compiles the other order to code that
+    * rounds differently (a replayed MSFS 2024 frame differed by up to 10/255
+    * in up to 2.9% of its pixels), which would hide real differences from a
+    * pixel comparison across driver versions. */
+   nir_foreach_block(block, impl) {
+      nir_foreach_instr(instr, block) {
+         if (instr->type != nir_instr_type_intrinsic)
+            continue;
+         nir_intrinsic_instr *intr = nir_instr_as_intrinsic(instr);
+         if (intr->intrinsic != nir_intrinsic_decl_reg)
+            continue;
+         const char *type = msl_uint_type(nir_intrinsic_bit_size(intr),
+                                         nir_intrinsic_num_components(intr));
+         P_IND(ctx, "%s r%u = %s(0);\n", type, intr->def.index, type);
+      }
+   }
 }
 
 /* Emitted as uint words rather than individual bytes to keep the
